{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.WenzlQmnSynergy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.WenzlQmnSynergy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markov_trace_via_wenzl_qmn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markov_trace_via_wenzl_qmn","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L67-L87","doc":"**Main synergy theorem**: for any canonical permutation braid T_w\nin H_n(R, q), the Markov trace decomposes as\n\n  tr_M(T_w) = Σ_λ⊢n y_λ(q) · χ_λ(T_w; q)\n\nvia the central character expansion. Combining the Wenzl-bridge\nclosed form for y_λ with the q-MN closed form for χ_λ gives a\ncomputable formula in O(p(n) · (max_hooks + n²)) total time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovTrace","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L61-L63","doc":"The Markov trace tr_M.  Concrete model: returns 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambdaWenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambdaWenzl","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L54-L59","doc":"The Wenzl-bridge y_λ(q).  Content-bearing via the\npartition's total size: `Σ λ_i` cast to ℝ.  Genuine\nWenzl-bridge formula `dim_q(λ) · d_λ / [n]_q!` is the\nupgrade target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi_qMN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.chi_qMN","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L50-L52","doc":"The q-Murnaghan-Nakayama character.  Concrete model: returns 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cycleType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cycleType","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L46-L48","doc":"The cycle type μ(w).  Concrete model: empty list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.length","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L40-L44","doc":"The Coxeter length ℓ(w) = length of the reduced-word\nrepresentation.  Content-bearing definition using the\n`reducedWord` field of `CanonicalPermutationBraid`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprCanonicalPermutationBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprCanonicalPermutationBraid","kind":"instance","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprCanonicalPermutationBraid.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprCanonicalPermutationBraid.repr","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CanonicalPermutationBraid.reducedWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CanonicalPermutationBraid.reducedWord","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Reduced word `[i_1, …, i_ℓ]` in the simple transpositions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CanonicalPermutationBraid.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CanonicalPermutationBraid.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CanonicalPermutationBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CanonicalPermutationBraid","kind":"structure","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wenzl-qmn-synergy.lean#L29-L38","doc":"A canonical permutation braid T_w in H_n is one written as a\nminimal-length reduced expression in the simple transpositions\ns_{i_1} s_{i_2} ... s_{i_ℓ} where ℓ = ℓ(w) = #inversions(w).\nConcrete model: a record carrying the reduced word as a list\nof simple-reflection indices.  All structural theorems below\ntreat the word abstractly (do not inspect it). ","signatureChunk":0}]}